            <div xml:id="d555">

                <pb facs="0562" n="552" sameAs="frus:frus1943v01/pg552"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 Moscow/19: Telegram</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Acting Secretary of State
                        to the Chargé in the Soviet Union</hi> (<hi
                            rendition="#italic">Hamilton</hi>)</head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1943-10-11T22:00:00-04:00">October 11,
                            1943—10 p.m.</date>
                    </dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>980. Your telegram No. 1587, Oct. 11, 10 a.m. There has been no announcement that
                    the Three-Power Conference is to be held in Moscow and no announcement that the
                    Secretary is heading our delegation. The British Embassy had informed us that it
                    had been jointly agreed with the Soviet Government that no announcement would be
                    made until the arrival at Moscow of the British and American delegations. We
                    concurred in this arrangement and are therefore at a loss to understand the
                    statements published in the British Daily Bulletin.</p>
                <closer>
                    <signed>[<hi rendition="#small-caps">Stettinius</hi>]</signed>
                </closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
